# Extensão REST Client do VS Code.
# 8080 = Gateway (padrão) | 8001 = Python | 8002 = Node | 8003 = Go | 8004 = Rust
# Para testar uma API direto, troque só a porta.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### Criar
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Ana Silva", "email": "ana@exemplo.com", "birthday": "2000-05-15", "cpf": "12345678901" }

### Listar
GET {{baseUrl}}/users

### Buscar
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/1

### Substituir
PUT {{baseUrl}}/users/1
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Ana Souza", "email": "ana@exemplo.com", "birthday": "2000-05-15", "cpf": "12345678901" }

### Atualizar parcial
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/users/1
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Ana S. Souza" }

### Remover
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/users/1

### --- Erros ---

### 400: campo inválido
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Ana", "email": "invalido", "birthday": "2000-05-15", "cpf": "12345678901" }

### 400: JSON inválido
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name":

### 400: id inválido
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/abc

### 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/999999

### --- Gateway (porta 8080) ---

### Health (o gateway repassa para uma das APIs)
GET http://localhost:8080/health

### Roteamento por header: força a API Rust (veja X-Upstream na resposta)
GET http://localhost:8080/users
X-Backend: api-rust

### Roteamento por path: /rust/users chega na API Rust como /users
GET http://localhost:8080/rust/users

### Ignora o cache (X-Cache: BYPASS)
GET http://localhost:8080/users
Cache-Control: no-cache

### Estado do gateway (upstreams, circuitos, cache, rate limit)
GET http://localhost:8080/_gateway/status

### Esvazia o cache do gateway
POST http://localhost:8080/_gateway/cache/flush
